  "problem": "Compute $\\text{E}[-2X-4]$ if $\\text{E}[X]=-\\frac{5}{2}.$",
  "worked_solution": "For any constants $a$ and $b$ and any random variable $X,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\text{E}[aX+b]=a\\text{E}[X]+b.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[-2X-4] & =-2\\text{E}[X]-4 \\\\  & =-2(-\\frac{5}{2})-4 \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
